{"assets":["/statement-assets/61e52cf6a19c60b32c4ebec0348580598fa70356318ef69fb76e0c80948e41a8.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"363","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Fence"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is a fence in front of Polycarpus's home. The fence consists of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" planks of the same width which go one after another from left to right. The height of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th plank is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"hi"},{"kind":"text","text":" meters, distinct planks can have distinct heights."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/61e52cf6a19c60b32c4ebec0348580598fa70356318ef69fb76e0c80948e41a8.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Fence for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n = 7"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h = [1, 2, 6, 1, 1, 7, 1]"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Polycarpus has bought a posh piano and is thinking about how to get it into the house. In order to carry out his plan, he needs to take exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" consecutive planks from the fence. Higher planks are harder to tear off the fence, so Polycarpus wants to find such "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" consecutive planks that the sum of their heights is minimal possible."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Write the program that finds the indexes of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" consecutive planks with minimal total height. Pay attention, the fence is not around Polycarpus's home, it is in front of home (in other words, the fence isn't cyclic)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 1.5·105, 1 ≤ k ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of planks in the fence and the width of the hole for the piano. The second line contains the sequence of integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h1, h2, ..., hn"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ hi ≤ 100"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"hi"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the height of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th plank of the fence."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print such integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":" that the sum of the heights of planks "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", ..., "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j + k - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the minimum possible. If there are multiple such "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":"'s, print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7 3\n1 2 6 1 1 7 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the sample, your task is to find three consecutive planks with the minimum sum of heights. In the given case three planks with indexes 3, 4 and 5 have the required attribute, their total height is 8."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"363B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/363/problem/B"}